Store backing: a namespace may declare, once, how it meets the disk, a mode word then a
path, at create or on the call channel. run keeps the value in the store alone; owned loads
the file at first use and writes every update and load through, by a temp file beside it
and a rename; shared does the same and reloads before a call whenever the file's time or
size moved since the last load. A forwarder declares to the owner up the channel, so a
sub-make that parses the same makefile joins the owner's backing; a repeat must match
the first declaration, and a different mode or path is refused.

